; The configuration binds C-c ? to help:describe-bindings and shows *Help*
; below the selected view, by help:buffer?.
> (eq? (keys:lookup client "C-c ?") help:describe-bindings)
#t
> (define notes (buffers:make "notes" "Buy milk.\n"))
> (layout:switch-to-buffer notes)
> (in-client (lambda () (help:describe-key "C-x C-f" (layout:selected-view))))
> (shown)
(("notes" #t) ("*Help*" #f))
> (help)
# C-x C-f runs the command file-picker:find-file, bound by (file-picker)
<file-picker:find-file> is a command in (file-picker).
It is on [C-x C-f].
Visits PATH and shows its buffer in the selected view.
> (in-client (lambda () (help:describe-name 'undo:limit (layout:selected-view))))
> (help)
# undo:limit
An option in (undo).
Its value here is 4000000; its setting is 4000000 and its default 4000000.
How large a buffer's history may grow: the characters its edits removed and inserted, plus 32 per edit. 0 keeps no history.
> (help:buffer? (help-buffer))
#t
> (help:buffer? notes)
#f
> (eq? help:name-category 'help:name-category)
#t
